      <p>III. The Services may not be used to store, transmit, or facilitate access to content or communications that are illegal, harmful, unwanted, inappropriate, or otherwise objectionable.</p>
      <p>IV. The Customer shall not use the Services to engage in any activity that is unlawful, deceptive, infringes on the rights of others, or is otherwise damaging to the operations, security, or reputation of 360 Degree Cloud.</p>
      <p>V. The Customer shall not attempt to bypass, disable, or exploit service limitations, security mechanisms, or filtering tools.</p>
      <p>VI. The Customer is solely responsible for evaluating whether the Services provide sufficient technical and legal safeguards for the Customer's intended use.</p>

      <h3>Opt-Out Compliance</h3>
      <p>In the event that any end-user client opts out of receiving messages or calls, it shall be the sole responsibility of the Client to ensure that no further communications are sent to such end-user. The Client must implement and maintain appropriate mechanisms to honor all opt-out requests in a timely and effective manner.</p>

      <h3>INDIA</h3>
      <p>I. The Customer agrees that all services availed from 360 Degree Cloud shall be used solely for lawful and valid business purposes. The Customer shall not use the services to generate or transmit any calls or SMS messages that violate applicable laws.</p>
      <p>II. The Customer further agrees that, upon request by 360 Degree Cloud, opt-in proof shall be furnished within forty-eight (48) hours.</p>
      <p>III. In the event of non-compliance, the Customer shall be liable to bear the penalty as determined at the sole discretion of 360 Degree.</p>

      <h3>COUNTRIES OTHER THAN INDIA</h3>
      <p>The Customer acknowledges and agrees to comply with all applicable regulations, industry standards, and 360 Degree Cloud's policies regarding the use of messaging services, including but not limited to the 10DLC (10-Digit Long Code) messaging framework.</p>
      <p>I. Messages sent prior to 10DLC verification: penalty of <strong>$10,000 USD</strong> per violation.</p>
      <p>II. Evasion of 10DLC messaging rules: penalty of <strong>$1,000 USD</strong> per instance.</p>
      <p>III. Third and subsequent content violations by the same Content Provider: penalty of <strong>$10,000 USD</strong> per incident.</p>
